  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Stack likes the number 333 a lot.\n\nHe has two non-negative integers AAA and BBB.\n\nIn one operation, Stack can do either of the following:\n\n\nA:=∣A−B∣A:=|A-B|A:=∣A−B∣ (change AAA to ∣A−B∣|A-B|∣A−B∣)\nB:=∣A−B∣B:=|A-B|B:=∣A−B∣ (change BBB to ∣A−B∣|A-B|∣A−B∣)\nNote that ∣X∣|X|∣X∣ denotes absolute value of XXX. For example ∣−7∣=7|-7| = 7∣−7∣=7 and ∣4∣=4|4| = 4∣4∣=4.\n\nFind the **minimum** number of operations after which **at least** one integer out of AAA and BBB becomes divisible by 333.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input contains a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nThe only line of each test case contains two integers AAA and BBB.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output in a single line the **minimum** number of operations after which **at least** one integer out of AAA and BBB becomes divisible by 333.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "0≤A,B≤1090 \\leq A, B \\leq 10^90≤A,B≤109"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2\n0 343\n1 1",
        "output": "0\n1",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: A=0A=0A=0 is already divisible by 333.\nTest case 222: In the only operation, Stack can change A=1A=1A=1 to A=∣A−B∣=∣1−1∣=0A = |A-B| = |1-1| = 0A=∣A−B∣=∣1−1∣=0. Now A=0A=0A=0 is divisible by 333."
      }
    ]
  },
